AB  - Section Overview of this article provides an overview of milestones in prenatal and infant development (from conception through 2. years of age and the emergence of language). Section Current Trends discusses current trends in the field with emphases on newer theories (e.g., dynamic system theories) and research, notably on the 'ecologies of infancy' (diversity of prenatal and infant development including the influences of culture and socioeconomic status, the effects of parenting, and nonparental care of infants) and on neurological brain assessments of infants. Section Future Directions concludes with consideration of future directions for the development of an integrated infant science. © 2015 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
