AB  - The proceedings contain 23 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Health Information Science. The topics include: Empowering Patients with HIPAA Aware Personal Health Libraries; Automatic Breast Lesion Segmentation Using Continuous Max-Flow Algorithm in Phase Preserved DCE-MRIs; research on Suicide Identification Method Based on Microblog “Tree Hole” Crowd; strengthen Immune System Based on Genetic Testing and Physical Examination Data; mining Outlying Aspects on Healthcare Data; multi-label Anomaly Classification Based on Electrocardiogram; Effective Tensor Based PCA Machine Learning Techniques for Glaucoma Detection and ASPP – EffUnet Classification; DEPRA: An Early Depression Detection Analysis Chatbot; machine Learning Algorithm for Analysing Infant Mortality in Bangladesh; Advancing Health Information System with System Thinking: Learning Challenges of E-Health in Bangladesh During COVID-19; applications and Challenges of Deep Learning in Computer Vision; generating Data Models to Manage Individual Information Related to Environmental Risk Factors and Social Determinants of Health; MKGB: A Medical Knowledge Graph Construction Framework Based on Data Lake and Active Learning; HMDFF: A Heterogeneous Medical Data Fusion Framework Supporting Multimodal Query; Developing Telerehabilitation in Low-Income Countries During COVID-19: Commencement and Acceptability of Telerehabilitation in Rohingya and Host Community People; Towards a User-Level Self-management of COVID-19 Using Mobile Devices Supported by Artificial Intelligence, 5G and the Cloud; Auto-correlation Based Feature Extraction Approach for EEG Alcoholism Identification; An Automatic Scheme with Diagnostic Index for Identification of Normal and Depression EEG Signals; ADHD Children Identification Based on EEG Using Effective Connectivity Techniques; Multi-BERT-wwm Model Based on Probabilistic Graph Strategy for Relation Extraction.
