AB  - Purpose of review: This article describes the evidence about why reading aloud to children is important to help them develop the language and early reading skills necessary for school readiness. Recent findings: This information supports the value of Reach Out and Read; physicians advising parents to read aloud. Conclusion: Reach Out and Read should be implemented in health care sites serving low-income children. © 2010 Wolters Kluwer Health | Lippincott Williams & Wilkins.
